Confirm with \cmd|pwd| that you are still in the disposable
\texttt{utp20} directory (compare it with the path in
\cmd|"$practice"|). Remove only the named files, and leave the
practice directory before removing it. If it is unexpectedly
nonempty, inspect it rather than forcing removal. If you entered
a separate \cmd|sh| for these examples, type \cmd|exit| afterwards.

\begin{terminal}
rm -i ./votes.txt ./tickets.txt
cd /tmp
rmdir "$practice"
\end{terminal}
